From e5951ae7be53a85074157d73a03838b2d2aca403 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Playport <dev@playport.invalid>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:42:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wow64: convert guest pointers through the iOS guest window

iOS has no low 4 GiB, so a WoW64 process's 32-bit address space is a
window at a host base: guest address g is host address base + g.
wow64_window.h holds the arithmetic (no Wine headers, so a host test
compiles it as is): guest to host keeps NULL, host to guest rejects a
pointer outside the window instead of truncating it. process_init
takes the base from the paired TEB32 and PEB32 (host address minus
guest address, the same for both); without a window they name the same
address and the base stays 0, which is Wine's usual identity.

The thunks convert through wow64_to_host and wow64_to_guest:
get_ptr and the 32-to-64 helpers (strings, object attributes, security
descriptors, ALPC, tokens), put_addr and every PtrToUlong of a host
pointer returned by a native call or into the guest's own buffer,
memory queries (checked against the guest address), the initial
thread context, and the exception, APC and callback frames. Values
the native side keeps for the guest stay guest values: thread start
and parameter, APC and completion contexts, exception and code
addresses, and the CPU module's bridge. A rejected pointer is logged
and the guest gets 0.

wow64win.dll does not convert yet: a guest win32u call ends the
process with STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED. Failed guest system calls, the
guest's NtTerminateProcess with its last 32 calls and callbacks, and
the images it maps (by the name its loader passes) are logged.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-03-portal2-wow64-pointers.md
Offered-upstream: no; the window exists only on the iOS port
